  "query_preview": "/Tuesday through Saturday/...\nA long wave trough will deepen into the Intermountain West \nthrough Wednesday, bringing cool temperatures and a low chance \nof showers on Wednesday into Thursday. The trough will then move\neast as a ridge of high pressure will develop over the western \nUS by the latter half of the week. Some model disagreement \ndelays the trough's exit out of the region, which would keep \ncool and wet conditions lingering through the end of the work \nweek. However, the bulk of model solutions keep the ridge of \nhigh pressure for the weekend, bringing above normal \ntemperatures and dry conditions likely for Friday into Saturday.",
